WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:04.660
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute Papers
with Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:04.660 --> 00:00:09.490
Whether a technique can be deemed as artificial
intelligence or not, is a question that I

00:00:09.490 --> 00:00:14.690
would like to see exiled from future debates
and argumentations. Of course, anyone may

00:00:14.690 --> 00:00:19.980
take part in any debate of their liking, I
would, however, like to point out the futility

00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:22.600
of such endeavors. Let me explain why.

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:27.769
Ever heard a parent and a son having an argument
whether the son is an adult or not?

00:00:27.769 --> 00:00:32.780
"You are not an adult, because adults don't
behave like this!" And arguments like that.

00:00:32.780 --> 00:00:37.190
The argument is not really about whether a
person is an adult, but it is about the very

00:00:37.190 --> 00:00:39.290
definition of an adult.

00:00:39.420 --> 00:00:45.220
Do we define an adult as someone who has common
sense and behaves responsibly? Or is it enough

00:00:45.229 --> 00:00:49.019
to be of 18 or 21 years old to be an adult?

00:00:49.019 --> 00:00:54.629
If we decide which definition we go for, the
scaffolding for the entire argument crumbles,

00:00:54.629 --> 00:00:59.059
because it is built upon a term for which
the definition is not agreed upon.

00:00:59.059 --> 00:01:03.879
I feel that we have it the same with artificial
intelligence in many debates.

00:01:03.879 --> 00:01:09.340
The definition of artificial intelligence,
or at least one possible definition, is the

00:01:09.340 --> 00:01:11.729
following:
Artificial intelligence (AI) is the intelligence

00:01:11.729 --> 00:01:14.630
exhibited by machines or software.

00:01:14.630 --> 00:01:19.359
It is a bit of a copout, so we have to go
and check the definition of intelligence.

00:01:19.359 --> 00:01:23.219
There are multiple definitions, but for the
sake of argument, we are going to let this

00:01:23.219 --> 00:01:24.210
one slip.

00:01:24.210 --> 00:01:29.560
One possible definition for intelligence is
"the ability to learn or understand things

00:01:29.560 --> 00:01:32.369
or to deal with new or difficult situations".

00:01:32.369 --> 00:01:39.549
Now, this sentence is teeming with ill-defined
terms, such as learn, understand things, deal

00:01:39.549 --> 00:01:42.499
with new situations, difficult situations.

00:01:42.499 --> 00:01:48.100
So, if we have a shaky definition of artificial
intelligence, it is quite possibly pointless

00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:53.770
to argue whether self driving cars can be
deemed artificially intelligent or not. Imagine

00:01:53.770 --> 00:01:59.060
two physicists arguing whether a material
is ferromagnetic, but none of them has the

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:04.179
slightest idea what magnetism means. If we look at it like this, it is very easy

00:02:04.179 --> 00:02:10.229
to see the futility of such arguments. If
we had as poorly crafted definitions in physics

00:02:10.229 --> 00:02:16.840
as we have for intelligence, magnetism would
be defined as "stuff pulling on other stuff".

00:02:16.840 --> 00:02:18.860
This is the first part of the argument.

00:02:18.860 --> 00:02:24.459
The second part is that artificial intelligence
is imagined to be a mystical thing that only

00:02:24.459 --> 00:02:30.190
exists in the future, or it may exist in the
present, but it has to be shrouded in mystery.

00:02:30.190 --> 00:02:36.510
Let me give you an example. The A* algorithm
used to be called AI and was (and still is)

00:02:36.510 --> 00:02:43.239
widely taught in AI courses at many universities.
A* is used in many pathfinding situations

00:02:43.239 --> 00:02:48.500
where we seek to go from A to B on a map in
the presence of possible obstacles. It is

00:02:48.500 --> 00:02:51.720
widely used in robotics and computer games.

00:02:51.720 --> 00:02:57.780
Nowadays, calling a pathfinding algorithm
AI is simply preposterous. It is a simple,

00:02:57.780 --> 00:03:01.200
well-understood technique that does something
we are used to.

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:05.540
Imagine someone waving their GPS device claiming
that there is AI in there.

00:03:05.540 --> 00:03:10.780
But back then, when it was new, hazy, and
poorly understood, we put it in a drawer with

00:03:10.780 --> 00:03:16.000
the label "AI" on it. As soon as people start
to understand it, they pull it out from this

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:21.519
drawer, and disgustedly claim, "Well, this
is not AI, it's just a graph algorithm.

00:03:21.519 --> 00:03:26.180
Graphs are not AI, that's just mathematics."
It is important to note that none of the

00:03:26.180 --> 00:03:31.310
techniques that we see today are mysterious
in any sense, the entirety of deep learning

00:03:31.310 --> 00:03:36.480
and everything else is a series of carefully
prescribed mathematical operations.

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:42.709
I will try to briefly assess the two arguments:
- Arguments about AI are not about the algorithms

00:03:42.709 --> 00:03:47.799
they seem to be discussing, but about the
very definition of AI, which is ill-defined

00:03:47.799 --> 00:03:51.560
at best.
- AI is imagined to be a mystical thing that

00:03:51.560 --> 00:03:57.000
only exists in the future, or it may exist
in the present, but it has to be, in some

00:03:57.000 --> 00:03:59.000
way, shrouded in mystery.

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:04.319
The good news is that using this knowledge,
we can easily defuse such futile arguments.

00:04:04.319 --> 00:04:08.950
If someone says that deep learning is not
artificial intelligence because all it does

00:04:08.950 --> 00:04:14.930
is matrix algebra, we can ask: "okay, what
is your definition of artificial intelligence?"

00:04:14.930 --> 00:04:20.450
If this person defines AI as being a sentient
learning being akin to humans, then we have

00:04:20.450 --> 00:04:24.980
immediately arrived to a conclusion that deep
learning is not AI.

00:04:24.980 --> 00:04:29.790
Let us not fool ourselves by thinking that
we are arguing about things when we are simply

00:04:29.790 --> 00:04:35.010
arguing about definitions. As soon as the
definition is agreed upon, the conclusion

00:04:35.010 --> 00:04:36.920
emerges effortlessly.

00:04:36.920 --> 00:04:41.000
Thanks for watching, and for your generous
support, and I'll see you next time!

